      "block_id": "2605.28615_p10_b8",
      "text": "GenEval 2. We further evaluate our method on GenEval 2 [17], a more challenging benchmark well-suited for\nmodern models. As shown in Table 5, compared to the baseline, BiDPO exhibits significant improvements in\nboth atomic-level (6.6%) and prompt-level (1.8%). This demonstrate that our BiDPO is robust to benchmark\ndrift.\n",
      "bbox": [
        70.87,
        341.22,
        541.41,
        390.29
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        283,
        1364,
        2165,
        1561
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.86,
      "font_name": "TeXGyrePagellaX-Bold",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 322,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.28615_p10_b9",
      "text": "Extending BiDPO to Modern MMDiT. We conduct experiments on the prevailing MMDiT architecture. As\nshown in Table 6, BiDPO brings significant improvements to SD3-Medium, particularly as compositional\ncomplexity increases. Notably, with the assistance of BiDPO, SD3-Medium even outperforms Flux. This\nvalidates that BiDPO is model-agnostic and can generalize well to current SOTA models.\n",
      "bbox": [
        70.59,
        397.14,
        541.14,
        446.24
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        282,
        1588,
        2164,
